{
  "id": "04-the-song-she-could-play",
  "title": "The Song She Could Play",
  "tenet": "Discipline turns gifts into fruit",
  "durationMs": 68686,
  "text": "Imagine two friends learning the keyboard. One can pick up a tune almost immediately. The other struggles, but practises for ten minutes each evening. Months pass. The first friend plays when she feels inspired; the second keeps her small appointment. Then a neighbour who is ill asks whether anyone can play her favourite hymn. The second girl sits beside her bed and plays it through. Her hands still tremble a little. But the song she practised has become comfort for someone else.\n\nDiscipline is how gifts become fruit. The question is not simply what you were given, but what you are doing with it. Stop comparing your field with another person's field. Work your own land. A small practice, repeated faithfully, prepares you to serve when the moment comes. The point is not applause for being disciplined. The point is that someone can be helped because you became ready.\n\nChoose one gift you can develop for service. Give it a small, realistic place in your day. Keep that appointment after the excitement fades. Practise today for the person you may help tomorrow.",
